From 9770ebde6ee2666afade8b9fde8c5cecd9235194 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:07:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] minicargo: a member's `features`/`optional` survive
 `workspace = true` in any key order

tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1 (crates/cli/Cargo.toml):

    tree-sitter-generate = { features = [ "load" ], workspace = true }

TOML doesn't order a table's keys, and taplo-formatted manifests sort them,
so `features` is read first.  The `workspace` key then replaced the whole
dependency with the workspace entry, dropping `load` (with a "Workspace
dependency already added?" warning): tree-sitter-generate was built
without its `load` feature, and with it the items the CLI calls
(`load_grammar_file`, node-types generation, `dep:semver`).  With the keys
the other way round it worked.  `optional = true` written before
`workspace` was lost the same way, making the dependency unconditional.

Keep the features and the optional flag read before `workspace` and merge
them into the inherited entry (cargo allows exactly these two keys next to
`workspace = true`).  The warning goes: the case it caught is this one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/minicargo/manifest.cpp | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/minicargo/manifest.cpp b/tools/minicargo/manifest.cpp
index 79db3982..9f394937 100644
--- a/tools/minicargo/manifest.cpp
+++ b/tools/minicargo/manifest.cpp
@@ -1150,15 +1150,19 @@ void PackageRef::fill_from_kv(
             if( !wm ) {
                 eh.error("Using workspace depdency with no loaded workspace");
             }
-            if( !was_added ) {
-                eh.warning("Workspace dependency already added?");
-            }
             const auto& src_deps = wm->dependencies();
             auto s_it = ::std::find_if(src_deps.begin(), src_deps.end(), [&](const auto& x) { return x.m_key == depname; });
             if( s_it == src_deps.end() ) {
                 eh.error("Unable to find dependency `", depname, "` in workspace");
             }
+            // `features` and `optional` are the keys a member may add to an inherited dependency, and TOML doesn't
+            // order a table's keys: ones read before `workspace` are merged in, not overwritten
+            // - tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1: `tree-sitter-generate = { features = [ "load" ], workspace = true }`
+            auto features = ::std::move(m_features);
+            bool optional = m_optional;
             *this = *s_it;
+            m_features.insert(m_features.end(), features.begin(), features.end());
+            m_optional |= optional;
         }
         return ;
     }
